{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And you were unwilling, etc.</b> And although the ten spoke their report, as it says nearby: ״אַחֵינוּ הֵמַסּוּ״ etc., HaShem had already told them that the conquest of the city is not from the side of Israel's might but as a gift from HaShem, as we examined precisely in parashat Shelach (Numbers 13:2) from the statement ״אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי נוֹתֵן״ — for He drives out the inhabitants of the land before them, as it also says nearby: ״HaShem etc. — He will fight for you.״ And there is no contradiction in this statement to deny the wondrous strength of the city and its people that the spies described; and with this the difficulty of the Ramban is not difficult."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:19.455481699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}